exact_texts.judge:
Two new figures in spikes/netcode-proof/crates/judge/src/figures.rs, each listed in FIGURES (:632-825) with unit "C62H-BOUND":
- Figure { name: "snap_lost_unexplained_count", compute: Some(snap_lost_unexplained_count), unit: "C62H-BOUND", what: "client-ticks filed lost that neither the room's record (no snapshot sent) nor the link's (a snapshot datagram lost) explains (-17)" }
- Figure { name: "snap_whole_despite_link_loss_count", compute: Some(snap_whole_despite_link_loss_count), unit: "C62H-BOUND", what: "client-ticks filed whole at which the link's record lost a snapshot datagram: the record overstated (-17)" }
A shared room-side reader does three things. It takes `clients` from the room logs' headers (one value, else a gap, as `decoded` does at figures.rs:328-343). It takes `hs.server_hash` through slot_hashes (:236-279). It takes `tick.s.snap_link_lost_count` from every room tick record. That last read is a gap when no room log gives the series, when a room tick record lacks it, when a list does not hold `clients` entries, or when an entry is below 0.
snap_lost_unexplained_count reads the client logs (the `decoded_hash` writers: process client or bots, :224-233), measured tick records only. For each (slot, tick) with snap_incomplete 1 (an entry other than 0 or 1 is a gap; so is a tick with no room record), it counts the pair when that slot's server_hash there is non-null and its snap_link_lost_count there is 0. It returns the count, and never Empty.
snap_whole_despite_link_loss_count reads the same records. For each (slot, tick) with a non-null decoded_hash other than 0, it counts the pair when the room's record gives that slot snap_link_lost_count 1 or more. A tick with no room record is skipped.
No change to eval.rs, marks.rs or main.rs for C62H-BOUND: figure checks already take parts (marks.rs:543-551, :585-591), and a figure gap already makes a non-failing run INVALID (eval.rs:1215-1231).
Fixtures go in crates/judge/tests/engine.rs, beside hash_mark and hash_log (:1296-1335):
- each explanation alone (a null server hash; a link loss of 1) reads 0;
- an unexplained tick reads 1;
- a warm-up tick is not counted;
- a whole hash with a link loss reads 1 on the second figure;
- the sentinel with a link loss reads 0;
- gaps make the run INVALID: the series missing from every room log, a room tick without it, a wrong-length list, a negative entry, an incomplete measured tick with no room record;
- a bite run whose figure fails reads shown.
JDG-ONLY-1's fix (main.rs:94, eval.rs:958-962) is not part of this design. Its standing home is 'npt-judge's next change', so it rides here, counted apart, unless the advisor rules otherwise (C62HB-Q5).

